      "editorial": {
        "en": {
          "why_it_matters": "This belongs on RADAR because the Charlie Parker frame lands on a collaboration with its own real history rather than a pickup tribute band. Herring and Alexander have been testing alto against tenor at Smoke for more than two decades, and their recordings from the room show how much of the music comes from friction, shared vocabulary, and instant response. Putting that relationship inside a Parker birthday week makes the lineage audible without turning it into museum repertory.",
          "trip_verdict": "Actively make room for one of the remaining sets if New York is already in play, especially if saxophone identity and hard-bop lineage are part of the trip. Five nights provide enough flexibility that I would not displace a genuinely singular premiere, farewell, or one-off to make it happen.",
